todd phillips joker movie has finally  cast two of the most recognizable  characters in the dc comics universe  but the choices may raise a few eyebrows  per comicbook.com child actor dante  pereira olsen is set to play a young  bruce wayne  years before he steps into the cape and  cowell to become batman  in 2015 pereira olson appeared briefly  in another comic book adaptation  marvel's jessica jones acclaimed british  actor douglas hodge will take on the  role of alfred pennyworth  a former special operations executive  operative and bruce's loyal butler and  later  legal guardian following the deaths of  thomas and martha wayne  pereira olsen's involvement with joker  reunites him with joaquin phoenix  who plays arthur fleck the failed  stand-up comedian who eventually turns  to a life of crime and becomes a joker  pereira olsen played a younger version  of phoenix's character  in the lynn ramsey's psychological  thriller you will never really hear  herrera olson will also act alongside  brett cullen who takes on the role of  thomas wayne cullen is perhaps best  known as goodwin from abc's lost and  briefly appeared in christopher nolan's  batman trilogy finale the dark knight  rises as a kidnapped congressman  traditionally batman plays a significant  role in the joker's transformation into  a deranged super  villain choosing a child actor to star  as bruce wayne opposite an adult who  plays the dude who snaps and starts  terrorizing gotham city  is a bold choice it subverts the idea  that the joker can't exist without  batman who committed himself to  vigilantism following the murders of his  parents  and that batman can't exist without the  joker no  no you you complete  me clearly if bruce in this universe  isn't even a preteen when joker is old  enough to have a failed career and a few  wrinkles on his face the joker doesn't  necessarily need a billionaire orphan in  a bat suit to make him the criminal he  is  but casting reports indicate that  cullen's role as thomas wayne will be  more than just flashback fodder  so perhaps a later act of the movie will  depict the shooting of the waynes  and plays some man who will be the joker  behind the trigger just as batman 89 did  on the other hand there's a notion that  bruce wayne and the joker are connected  not by death but by life  through none other than thomas wayne  himself casting reports and industry  gossip hints that the joker's mother  could play a big part in the film  and one fan theory speculates that  batman and the joker  will be secret half siblings sure this  theory is more than a little out there  but it does hold some weight  in the film thomas wayne is reportedly a  far less sympathetic character  than he usually is instead of a talented  physician and kind philanthropist who  does right by all he's reportedly a  quote cheesy and tanned businessman who  is more in the mold of a 1980s donald  trump who runs the mayor of gotham city  arthur might be so overtaken with  anguish and confusion following the  revelation that thomas is his father  that he grabs a gun and shoots his  biological father and his wife bruce's  mother martha  as a way to gain retribution for growing  up without a father and to make young  bruce hurt in the same way he did  or it might turn out that alfred  pennyworth and the wayne family won't  play that larger role in the upcoming  joker film  appearing in limited or even cameo  capacities rather than as crucial  characters  after all the movie is all about arthur  fleck and his eventual change into the  joker  described as quote an exploration of a  man disregarded by society  that is not only a gritty character  study but also a broader cautionary tale  find out the truth when joker hits  theaters october 4th  2019.
 

